WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.048 --> 00:00:07.041
Daisy and Kaleem walked up to the farmhouse with Finn.

2
00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:16.521
Daisy was nervous. "We probably shouldn't be here without permission."

3
00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:20.875
Just then a woman hurried around the side of the farmhouse.

4
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:25.514
"Oh, hello. I thought I heard a dog.

5
00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:29.220
I'm Jan. Do you kids live nearby?

6
00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:31.642
My husband and I are new in town.

7
00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:35.229
We bought this little farm a month ago."

8
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:40.155
Kaleem smiled. "You work at the library in town, right?

9
00:00:40.156 --> 00:00:44.960
So does my mom. I met you last week when I was there."

10
00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:51.820
"I remember now," Jan said. "Nice to see you again, Kaleem."

11
00:00:51.821 --> 00:00:57.151
Daisy patted Finn. "Our friend Finn picked up a new scent and led us here.

12
00:00:57.152 --> 00:01:01.205
Do you have any unusual animals on the farm?"

13
00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:08.065
Jan chuckled. "We brought our newest one home this afternoon.

14
00:01:08.066 --> 00:01:10.180
Would you like to see him?"

15
00:01:10.181 --> 00:01:12.749
"Yes," Daisy said.

16
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:27.099
Jan led the way around the house.

17
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:32.143
When they reached the farmyard, Daisy smiled at all the animals there.

18
00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:35.251
Some chickens were pecking around.

19
00:01:35.252 --> 00:01:38.261
A cat was sleeping in the sun.

20
00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:41.662
Goats and sheep were playing in a pen.

21
00:01:41.663 --> 00:01:45.149
Another pen held two miniature donkeys.

22
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:52.996
A short distance away, there was a lush pasture where two horses and a cow were grazing.

23
00:01:52.997 --> 00:01:56.484
Suddenly Daisy heard a strange sound.

24
00:01:56.485 --> 00:01:59.394
A man appeared from the barn.

25
00:01:59.395 --> 00:02:04.800
He was leading a tall, shaggy creature who was shrieking with alarm.

26
00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:08.538
Kaleem gasped. "Is that a . . . ?"

27
00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:13.428
"Meet our new llama, Floyd!" Jan grinned.

28
00:02:13.429 --> 00:02:15.984
"Isn't he cute?"

29
00:02:15.985 --> 00:02:21.390
Now Daisy knew exactly what "monster" the animals had seen!

30
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:24.885
Floyd was enormous, with a very long neck.

31
00:02:24.886 --> 00:02:29.356
His expression was sour. He shrieked again.

32
00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:33.214
"I don't hear any words from him," Daisy thought.

33
00:02:33.215 --> 00:02:39.190
"I think it's because he's so upset."

34
00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:45.683
"Would somebody tell that thing to be quiet?" the cat said, waking up from her nap.

35
00:02:45.684 --> 00:02:50.099
The man was struggling to lead the llama toward the donkeys' pen.

36
00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.818
"That's my husband, Jon," Jan said.

37
00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:59.317
"It looks like he's having trouble with Floyd."

38
00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:04.326
Daisy wondered why the llama was so upset.

39
00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:16.659
While Kaleem asked Jan about the donkeys, Daisy slipped away.

40
00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:21.802
"Excuse me," she whispered over the fence of the goat and sheep pen.

41
00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:24.204
"Do you like living on this farm?"

42
00:03:24.205 --> 00:03:27.879
The goat looked surprised that Daisy was talking to him.

43
00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.998
But he answered her question.

44
00:03:29.999 --> 00:03:35.636
"We love it! Our people feed us good food.

45
00:03:35.637 --> 00:03:40.666
And look at this rock pile they made for us to play on."

46
00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.801
He bounded away.

47
00:03:42.802 --> 00:03:45.497
That was enough to convince Daisy.

48
00:03:45.498 --> 00:03:48.592
This was a nice farm where animals were happy.

49
00:03:48.593 --> 00:03:53.617
She had to convince Floyd to calm down and tell her what was wrong.

50
00:03:53.618 --> 00:03:57.555
"I might be able to help," Daisy said.

51
00:03:57.556 --> 00:04:04.766
"I'm, uh, good with animals. Hello, Floyd."

52
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.743
The llama looked away.

53
00:04:06.744 --> 00:04:10.609
"You're very cute," Daisy said softly.

54
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:17.431
As she stepped closer to Floyd, Finn barked, "Don't get too close to that monster!"

55
00:04:17.432 --> 00:04:21.439
"Who are you calling a monster?" the llama snapped.

56
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.732
He spat out a wad of saliva. "Stay back, you noisy mutt!"

57
00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:35.891
Suddenly Floyd took off, ripping the rope out of Jon's hands!

